Keeps the unified capture pipeline that all the astro cameras share — the common acquisition layer above any one device.

The capture / acquisition layer of the astro estate: the *unified* pipeline that turns "a camera pointed at the sky" into frames on disk, shared across every instrument (astro-polecam, astro-eclipticam, astro-canon). It owns the common machinery — capture scheduling, night/session structure, frame naming and hand-off to storage — as distinct from the per-device specifics (which live in each [[astro-canon]]-style camera keeper) and from the downstream processing/science (which lives in [[astro-science]]). Three-layer split: astro-<camera> = device specifics, astro-capture = unified capture, astro-science = pipeline + deliverables.
